// use-midblock-parse-errors.ta — negative test: `use` can only appear at
// the start of a block (after optional let/use forms), because the desugar
// wraps the REST of the block in a lambda. A use in any later position has
// nothing to wrap, so it must be rejected as a parse error instead of
// leaking the internal ((use . bind) ...) form into the AST.
fn pa() { 1 }
fn main() {
  foo()
  use k <- pa()
  print(k)
}